{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-12T21:09:20.732Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6cac702086723f6d9ab0b467","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1713"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1713: strict create offers no auditable deferred value, so importers cannot create an item whose deadline, assignee or acceptance criteria are not known yet"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH-1713 (filed 2026-11-12). Under the strict preset, strict create requires concrete values for deadline, assignee and acceptance criteria and refuses every way of saying a value is not known yet: the repeatable options accept an explicit clear, but the three required scalars refuse --unset and accept no deferred value. An importer that mirrors records from another system (pm-github gated issue sync, Linear, ADO or CSV importers) must either fail or invent a deadline and an assignee. pm-github runs its sync inside one atomic import, so in a strict tracker every new GitHub issue fails strict create and the whole daily sync rolls back; one fleet repository has failed this way on every run for 19 days (importer side tracked in unbraind/pm-github issue 237). Proposed direction from the issue: an explicit, auditable deferred state for strict-required scalars on create, never a silent bypass. A typed marker or a defer option with a reason (CLI and SDK create options), recorded in history; pm health and pm validate list deferred fields as curation work; strict close still requires concrete values so a deferral never lets incomplete work finish; optionally the deferral is allowed only for items with external provenance or for callers that declare an import capability."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["gh:1713","governance","importers","sdk","strict-preset"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-12T21:09:20.732Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-12T21:09:20.732Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":240},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Strict create accepts an explicit deferral for deadline, assignee and acceptance criteria with a reason, through the CLI and the SDK create options; The deferral is recorded in history and pm validate and pm health list deferred fields as curation work; Strict close still requires concrete values for every deferred field; A strict-preset importer run creates items without inventing values and the pm-github sync no longer rolls back"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-33cw"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"An importer creates a strict item with explicitly deferred fields"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Strict create refuses every unknown deadline, assignee or acceptance criteria"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"efd0ff2e2f6368c2b3b421bc667c06faa04a6e620b06bff37163bd1d818e325b","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d927f5a1c381ec0573438b1538d93711de28669d09118a5c22a0042366d02f38"}
