{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-14T04:32:04.758Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9d7f970542d8df5a0a6bdb3b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1713","claim:pm-gh1719","lineage:pm-gh1713","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1713+pm-gh1719","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1713","claim:pm-gh1719","lineage:pm-gh1713","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-14T04:32:04.758Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-14T04:32:04.757Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Design (2026-11-14): deferral is typed item metadata deferred_fields [{field, reason}] (src/core/item/deferred-fields.ts declares the deferrable set as data: deadline, assignee, acceptance_criteria, estimated_minutes; repeatables already have --clear-*). Stored deferrals require item format 4, so a host that predates them refuses the record instead of dropping the entries and letting strict close pass. Create: --defer (repeatable, comma lists) + required --defer-reason (SDK defer[]/deferReason, MCP pm_create), parsed in src/sdk/lifecycle/create-deferrals.ts; a deferred option satisfies the strict required check; deferring a field also set or unset is create_deferral_conflict; a deferral drops the template default like an unset. Resolution: mutateItem prunes any entry whose field gained a value on the same write (covers update, update-many, claim, stdin-json). Close: outstanding deferrals refuse --validate-close strict with close_validation_deferred_fields (recovery is a runnable pm update) and warn otherwise. Curation: validate --check-metadata adds details.deferred_fields + validate_metadata_deferred_fields:<n>; health reports integrity details.curation informationally only, so strict fleet trackers running pm health --check-only in CI do not turn red. Creating directly in a terminal status with a deferral is allowed (it mirrors work finished elsewhere) and stays listed as curation work."}]}],"before_hash":"3c9db9274e4cfebc751ac1eb2c5d77dcedac03957a59ff368d901005fb75ffce","after_hash":"8fe29b7db8ee2501918962e1af2111dcd34145b4e4813e6bb12280c9810cc7be","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"673a89c4357e459d32863e8a522f3abf800f6b015dd5c8c42a76b7aefc6128ed"}
